1.1 Problem Statement
Creating a comic requires three distinct skills: writing a story, laying out panels, and illustrating them. Non-artists drop out at the illustration step, which is the least forgiving of the three. Existing tools solve only one part of the problem — text generators produce scripts but no panels, and image generators produce single pictures with no narrative continuity between them.

1.2 Brainstormed Ideas
#	Idea	Description
1	Text-only comic script generator	LLM writes a panel script; user illustrates it themselves
2	Image-only generator with manual captions	User generates images and types captions into a template
3	Single-model story + image tool	One model handles both text and imagery
4	Two-LLM + diffusion pipeline	Flash outlines, Pro narrates, Stable Diffusion illustrates
5	Interactive panel editor	Pipeline plus drag-and-drop panel rearrangement and caption rewriting
6	Community comic library	Shared gallery of generated comics with public profiles
7	Multi-page arc generator	Long-form comics across several issues with character memory
1.3 Prioritisation Criteria
Impact on the core illustration barrier · implementation effort · dependency on external APIs · fit with the five-milestone plan · risk.

