1.5 Prioritisation Outcome
Idea 4 sits first. It removes the illustration barrier outright at moderate effort, and splitting outline generation from narration generation is what makes the output feel coherent — a structured 5-panel skeleton constrains the story model so narration stays anchored to the panels instead of drifting into prose. That structural insight costs nothing extra in infrastructure, which is why it beats the higher-scope ideas on value-per-effort.

Idea 2 is deliberately deferred, not dropped. The modular service design (each pipeline stage in its own file) is what keeps it reachable in a later version.

Ideas 3 and 7 were rejected. No current model handles both text and imagery well enough to justify collapsing the pipeline, and long-form arcs multiply API cost and failure surface before the single-comic case is proven.

1.6 Key Ideation Insight
The bottleneck in comic creation is not creativity — it is execution skill. Users arrive with the story already in mind. The product's job is therefore to accept a rough premise plus preference fields and return something finished, not to help the user write.
